<title>RUSSIA: Russia Feb nickel output up, aluminium down mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Russia Feb nickel output up, aluminium down mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian nickel output in February rose seven percent on January's level, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The committee also said February primary aluminium production slipped eight percent on January levels. It gave no absolute production figures, but provided the following data:  </p>
<p>RUSSIAN NON-FERROUS AND PRECIOUS METALS OUTPUT</p>
<p>	 (all figures expressed as percentage changes)</p>
<p>			    Feb 1997	  Jan-Feb 1997    Feb 1996</p>
<p>			   pct change	 pct change	pct change</p>
<p>			   mth/mth  yr/yr   yr/yr	     yr/yr</p>
<p>Alumina		  -6.0     -0.5    -3.0		+6.0</p>
<p>Primary aluminium    -8.0     -2.0    +1.0	     +10.0</p>
<p>Copper concentrate  +13.0    -11.0   -16.0		+9.0</p>
<p>Refined copper	 -8.0    -13.0    -6.0		+5.0</p>
<p>Nickel		   +7.0     +1.0    -1.0		+1.0</p>
<p>Cobalt		  -10.0     +5.0   +15.0	     -19.0</p>
<p>Zinc		    +18.0     +9.0    -7.0	     +25.0</p>
<p>Gold		    -19.0    +20.0   +34.0		-2.0</p>
<p>Magnesium and</p>
<p>magnesium alloys    -11.0     -7.0    -4.0	     +13.0</p>
<p>Titaniun sponge     -11.0    +55.0   +59.0	     +23.0</p>
<p>Rolled aluminium     -5.0    -26.0   -21.0	     -40.0</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
